<content><![CDATA[<p>In this exercise, you will practice polygonal modeling fundamentals and using reference images to create a chess piece</p>
<oer-iframe src="https://youtube.com/embed/videoseries?list=PLcAjW37cz5QliQriwysglJwRIE6R8NP2f" title="Modeling a Basic Knight Tutorial"></oer-iframe>
<h2>Learning Objectives</h2>
<ol>
<li>Practice working from reference images</li>
<li>Practice using 3D software interface and terminology.</li>
<li>Use modeling workflows to create high quality topology and edge flow.</li>
<li>Familiarize yourself with a cumulative number of hotkeys and operations (it's a good idea to keep a personal log of hotkeys and operators that you will likely use again, as you go).</li>
</ol>
<h2>Instructions</h2>
<p>This is the most basic of four demonstrations on how to complete the Knight assignment.&nbsp;
If you complete this version you will receive full credit for this week's requirement to create a Knight for you Chess Set
However, you are expected to watch all three demonstrations.&nbsp;
They will show you how you might use new tools and methods to make your knight more unique or figurative.</p>
